{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Before he had finished speaking.</b> Meaning: while he was still saying ״עִם אֲדוֹנִי״ — and behold Rebekah! And this is a verse that comes as a sign, that she is the one suited to be with his master." "<b>Rebekah was going out.</b> Meaning: her going out from the well was caused by Eliezer's prayer. HaShem brought it about that she went out at that very moment — not before and not after — so that he would not stumble in another woman, for she is the one <b>who was born to Bethuel</b>, etc.; she is the destined match for Isaac, as I explained in the portion of Vayera at the verse (Genesis 22:20) ״וַיְהִי אַחֲרֵי וגו׳ וַיֻּגַּד לְאַבְרָהָם״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:01.586692667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}